  No uncensored HCI-nonresponse-to-USB-loss transition was observed.
  Every HCI-nonresponse window was ended by intervention, a reset of
  known treatment or unknown origin, or shutdown. Therefore
  the fault's untreated trajectory is UNKNOWN — not 45-66s, not
  indefinite. The experiment that settles it is a boot left
  strictly alone after BT-1 until the device leaves the bus.
